# -prev calibration snapshots are seeded by scripts/integrity-check-nightly.mjs
# on first run; drift detection compares current vs prev locally. Gitignored
# because on fresh clone the integrity-check seeds from the tracked canonical
# file (no false-positive drift on first nightly run after a checkout).
data/*-calibration-prev.json
# *.bak files anywhere — stale backups; never commit. Real backups live in
# data/cv-archives/ (gitignored separately) or in git history itself.
# *.bak-* covers date-suffixed backups produced by the launchd plist sweep
# scripts (e.g. com.mitchell.career-ops.foo.plist.bak-2026-05-23T...).
*.bak
*.bak-*
# Contaminated-content quarantine sinks (de-contamination sweeps 2026-05-30/31).
# Hold pre-scrub copies of hm-intel / popout / cv content — personal data with
# forbidden-metric phrasing. Dir-level ignore so a stray `git add -A` can never
# stage them (contents are also *.bak-ignored, but the dirs were not dir-ignored).
data/contaminated-*quarantine*/

# Scrub-backups (scripts/scrub-fabrications.mjs:34) — pre-scrub copies of apply-pack
# artifacts / popout JSONs / story drafts. Each backup holds BOTH Mitchell's personal
# career narrative AND the exact retired-metric fabrications the scrubber removes
# ("three production LLM agents", "99% fidelity", "600+ L8+"). A stray `git add -A`
# would leak both the personal data and the very fabrications being scrubbed from the
# public-facing corpus. Dir glob covers the dated dir, the -PRISTINE-PASS1 sibling, and
# any future-dated variant. Keep the backups on disk — they are the scrubber's audit trail.
data/scrub-backups*/
data/scrub-backups*

